@startuml
'==== Title ====
title "As a User, I want to use a Web UI to put for %n()sale a publication in my library in a direct sale." %n() SD


'==== basic style ====
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam objectFontSize 20
skinparam backgroundColor CornSilk
skinparam objectBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFE0
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3B4953
skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor black
hidefootbox
autonumber


' ==== Actor and participants ====
actor "User"
participant ":Client" as Client
participant ":Server" as Server
database "DB" as DB


User -> Client : I want to put an item %n()in my library on direct sale
activate Client
Client -> Server : GET /items/my-library {...}
activate Server
Server -> DB : select items in %n()user's library
DB --> Server : data
Server --> Client : 200 [ItemResponseDTO + links]
note right of Client
Each item includes:
- self
- create-direct-sale only if item
 can be put on direct sale
Client populates the dropdown only
with items containing create-direct-sale
end note
deactivate Server
Client --> User : Displays direct sale form %n() with items NotOnSale only
deactivate Client




User -> Client : Submit selected itemId, price, %n()currency, and time limit
activate Client
Client -> Server : POST {href from rel="create-direct-sale"}\n{ itemsId, priceValue, priceCurrency, %n()timeLimitSeconds }
note right of Server
Creates DirectSale and updates %n()Item saleStatus as OnDirectSale
end note
Server -> DB : insert sale / %n() update item
DB --> Server : success
Server --> Client : 201 Created
deactivate Server
Client --> User : The item was successfully %n()put on direct sale.
deactivate Client


/'Client -> Server : PATCH /my-library/{itemId} %n(){ "saleStatus" : "OnDirectSale"}
activate Client
activate Server
Server -> DB : select
DB --> Server : data
Server --> Client : 200 {...}
deactivate Server
deactivate Client'/


@enduml